From 098928a3090e7f3dbfa450f41a4fb3da1b029b9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:58:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] ASoC: ak4961: stage 1, power-up, SLIMbus enumeration
 and SPI registers

The AK4961 (ZTE Axon 7 main codec) as a SLIMbus driver (slim1dd,4961,
PGD and IFD) whose registers go over SPI on BLSP2 QUP3, as ZTE runs it
(CIF1 low): LDO, CIF, reset and the 9.6 MHz MCLK (PM8994 DIV_CLK1), then
on SLIMbus UP the device code check and the PGD port arrays.

Tested: PGD LA 0x85, IFD LA 0x86, device code 0x61 over SPI. No sound
card part yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i64chehV1XxwjxyaGp
